      "writtenOn": "2022-01-11T15:04:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi!\n\nI\u0027m curious why new TC, PRL, PE state machines are needed for ServoV4P1? How they are different from state machines used by Chromebooks?",
      "revId": "d052d4b0c319bf17800a5b6df344aa9cbc70bc50",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e81d5a5d_2970f5cd",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1149894
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-11T17:13:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To get the state machines to fit on the ServoV4p1, I changed the way timers work, ripped out Chromebooks related code that\u0027s unnecessary for ServoV4p1. Originally, I added config flags to comment out that code but things began to look very messy.",
      "parentUuid": "0ee520cc_b6c2b77d",
      "revId": "d052d4b0c319bf17800a5b6df344aa9cbc70bc50",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7538915d_6091ca76",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-11T18:58:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d strongly prefer we share these as much as possible to avoid double-maintenance.  That, plus it\u0027s not massively inspiring while we upstream our stack if we can\u0027t at least use our stack for all our own tools.  \n\nDouble maintenance on the PRL might not be too bad because it\u0027s relatively stable, but in the PE and TC it could definitely become a pain.",
      "parentUuid": "e81d5a5d_2970f5cd",
      "revId": "d052d4b0c319bf17800a5b6df344aa9cbc70bc50",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5b0a7c5e_b1ffc3c9",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1149894
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-11T20:24:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I generally agree with you but resources on the servoV4.1 and a typical chromebook are vastly different and would require many #ifdefs or IS_ENABLES be added to the TCPMv2 stack and could start looking much like the TCPMv1.\n\nOnce the ServoV4.1 USBC Stack stabilizes, it\u0027s unlikely to need changing because the hardware won\u0027t change. Unlike TCPMv2 for chromebooks that\u0027s getting constant updates because of newer hardware.\n\nAlso, I look at the servoV4.1 as being closer to CTVPD devices than a chromebooks and the CTVPD has its own tc and pe implementations. But we could probably keep PRL common to all implementation.",
      "parentUuid": "7538915d_6091ca76",
      "revId": "d052d4b0c319bf17800a5b6df344aa9cbc70bc50",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2aa0a089_00e69a2c",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-11T23:47:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Re: resources, is that even with the space freed up by removing RW?\n\nWhat parts of the stack in this CL are Servo-specific from a functional point of view?",
      "parentUuid": "5b0a7c5e_b1ffc3c9",
      "revId": "d052d4b0c319bf17800a5b6df344aa9cbc70bc50",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
