      "writtenOn": "2022-01-12T01:53:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Even with the uneven RO/RW split, building TCPMv2 for servoV4p1 exceeded the available flash. The TCPMv2 code has changed since the last time I built it for servoV4p1 and it no longer builds without errors. But I did see the following:\n\nbuild/servo_v4p1/RO/ec.RO.elf section `.bss\u0027 will not fit in region `IRAM\u0027\nNot enough space for shared memory.\nregion `IRAM\u0027 overflowed by 2088 byte\n\nNote that the ServoV4p1 uses the stm32f072 that has 16K Ram and 128K flash.\n\nThis is the build output with this CL:\n\n *** 12468 bytes in flash and 1028 bytes in RAM still available on servo_v4p1 RO\n *** 1724 bytes in flash and 7392 bytes in RAM still available on servo_v4p1 RW\n \n \nFrom what I can remember, I stripped out the following:\nTimer Code, flag_bit_names, cable probing, Charge Through States, LowPower stuff, Super States for RD and RP, TrySrc and TrySnk.\nFor PE, TCPMv2 has 69 non-PD3.0 states and I reduced that to 17.",
      "parentUuid": "2aa0a089_00e69a2c",
      "revId": "d052d4b0c319bf17800a5b6df344aa9cbc70bc50",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
